        },
        "body": {
          "type": "body",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The English Springer is a creature of two states: the field and the floor. The first is well-documented; the second, less so. A note on what the Springer does between the cover and the kitchen — and why it matters.</p>",
            "style": "editorial-body",
            "align": "left",
            "margin_bottom": 32
          }
